{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>If these men die the death of every man, etc.</b> In tractate Nedarim (39b) Resh Lakish said: there is an allusion to visiting the sick from the Torah, as it says: ״אִם כְּמוֹת כָּל הָאָדָם״ etc. — that they are ill and confined to their beds, and people come to visit them, ״לֹא ה׳ שְׁלָחָנִי״. And Rashi explained that he relied on the end of the verse, which says: ״וּפְקֻדַּת כָּל הָאָדָם יִפָּקֵד עֲלֵיהֶם״ — this פְּקִידָה means visiting. And behold, there is room for me to explain this פְּקִידָה in another way. For there are two kinds of benefit in this visiting: one is that they check after the needs of the sick person; the second is for the sake of those who go there, for just as it is good to go to a house of mourning so that the living will take it to heart, so too it is good to go to the sick person, for through this one will seek and examine one's deeds. For there go there the stout-hearted who are far from righteousness, who have no fear of Elohim before their eyes, and whose uncircumcised heart is blocked from understanding their latter end — that it is vanity and its end is unto the place of the maggot. And this is ״פְּקֻדַּת כָּל הָאָדָם״: that the end — which is the פְּקֻדַּת כָּל אָדָם — ״יִפָּקֵד״ upon them, ״יִפָּקֵד״ in the sense of remembering; that is to say, if the פְּקֻדַּת כָּל אָדָם — which is death — is remembered and reckoned upon them, and this is surely through visiting them, then this merit will redound to the many through them, and they do not receive punishment according to their measure — then according to their own words it is so, that לֹא ה׳ שְׁלָחָנִי. But if HaShem creates a creation, etc., and they do not die as is the way of all the world, then the פְּקֻדַּת כָּל הָאָדָם will not be remembered through them, for one does not learn from a novelty — for it would not enter a person's heart to die by such an unusual death. By this they will know that these men have spurned HaShem, and they are not worthy that any merit for others should redound through them." "And the reason for such a death: according to what I wrote above, that they denied the creation of the world anew and its having been created, Moses said: ״אִם בְּרִיאָה״ — if there truly was a new creation during the six days of creation, then HaShem will validate my words and will now create something new on earth, and through it they will recognize and know that HaShem makes new things. And that which was created through this creation was specifically because our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Avot 3:2): Were it not for the fear of the government, men would swallow each other alive. And they did not want any leader, for they said: ״כָל הָעֵדָה כֻּלָּם קְדוֹשִׁים וּבְתוֹכָם ה׳ וּמַדּוּעַ תִּתְנַשְּׂאוּ עַל קְהַל ה׳״. And according to their misguided reasoning, each man would swallow his fellow alive. Therefore they are punished according to their measure: that they descend to Sheol alive. For even one who is remiss in his eulogy of a person — our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Shabbat 105a) that he is worthy of being buried alive, because it appears that he does not feel the loss of the great man who cast his fear upon creatures — how much more so the congregation of Korah, who with a full mouth declared that they do not want any man elevated over them at all. Therefore Moses said that if they die on their beds and do not descend to Sheol alive, then לֹא ה׳ שְׁלָחָנִי to make all the appointments of the offices of leadership and the governance of the people. But if they descend to Sheol alive, by this they will know that they were measured according to their measure — that HaShem sent me to make all the appointments, so that all this people, each man in his place, may come in peace. Therefore it says ״וַיֹּאבְדוּ מִתּוֹךְ הַקָּהָל״: since HaShem desired that all Israel be in one congregation and in one unified group, and every congregation and assembly needs a leader so that no man swallow his fellow, and they did not want this — therefore they were destroyed. For he came to divide, and through his discord he separates between brothers."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:41:52.725346073Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}